        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "95bb9e53-7d8a-57b2-8c2b-188657a67233",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Benn F. Reyes, Stanley Kubrick\n- Films: Lolita, Dr. Strangelove or: How I Learned to Stop Worrying and Love the Bomb\n- Topics: public relations, movies, Cold War, nuclear conflict satire\n\nFacts:\n- Benn F. Reyes was born in San Francisco in 1915 and died in Stockholm, Sweden, in 1968.\n- Benn F. Reyes was an American publicist and impresario mainly known for his work in movies.\n- Benn F. Reyes's best-known movie ventures were collaborations with American director Stanley Kubrick.\n- Benn F. Reyes collaborated with Stanley Kubrick on the films Lolita and Dr. Strangelove or: How I Learned to Stop Worrying and Love the Bomb.\n- Dr. Strangelove or: How I Learned to Stop Worrying and Love the Bomb is a 1964 political satire black comedy film.\n- Dr. Strangelove satirizes Cold War fears of a nuclear conflict between the Soviet Union and the United States.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
